# The Project Transition

@body

- Your individual projects are complete.
- Now use the pitches, feedback, and executive summaries to choose a shared company.
- *Nov 12:* groups formed.
- [*Tonight, Nov 19: Company Vision Report (Form) due.*]{color=red} Submit once per group on Blackboard.
- *Dec 10:* group presentations.
- *Dec 17:* group business plan due.

=== layout: one-panel

# This Week's Work

@body

- Set #7: Bioethics in Biotechnology.
- Choose one product and submit the Company Vision Report (Form) tonight.
- Homework 6 is assigned. Check Blackboard for instructions and the deadline.
- Use the break to develop your product's science, competition, and milestones.

=== layout: two-panels

# Talking Points Guide

@left

- Edit and update your slide
- Add several pictures and some text
- It is best to have as few words as possible on your slide -- you do the talking not your slide
- Be prepared to give a *60 second presentation* about each of your assigned talking point

@right

- define the talking point, describe its relation to biotechnology, or provide a recent example of the talking point in biotechnology news
- Try to be unique
- Don't just copy the book, use the internet for research.
- Provide your own perspective

=== layout: one-panel

# Talking Points Guide

@body

- Please put into your own words
- It is okay if you read your notes, but put notes in your own words
- No direct quoting of an article, wikipedia or the textbook
- Minimize jargon
- Show ENTHUSIASM when you talk and make it exciting!

